{# gfadmin/templates/admin/form.html, rendered with page_title "New Need"
   (gfadmin/views.py:1922) -- the create half of Django's one need_form
   view. admin/need_form.njk in this same directory is the edit half; the
   two are separate templates here only because they were built in
   different work packages, and the follow-up that merges them is in the
   WP 6.8 wiring notes. Field NAMES are identical in both, so one POST
   handler could serve both the moment they merge.

   Bulma classes are copied from what django-bulma's `{{ form|bulma }}`
   filter emits for each widget type (div.field > label.label >
   div.control > .input/.textarea/.checkbox), rather than from the Django
   template, which only ever writes the filter.

   FIXES admin/form.html:31-37's dead food-bank preview (defect D2):
   views.py:1926-1928 resolves `foodbank` from `?foodbank=` and then never
   puts it in template_vars (1941-1945), so the second column that block
   was written for has never rendered on this page in production. Restored
   here -- through the port's own safe proxy signature
   (`?foodbank=<slug>&field=<known field>`, routes/admin/proxy.ts), never
   Django's raw `?url=` SSRF that WP 6.3 already replaced.
   `field=url` is the food bank's own website, matching what
   admin/form.html:33 asked for (`{{ foodbank.url|urlencode }}`). #}
{% extends "admin/page.njk" %}

{% block title %}{{ page_title }}{% endblock %}

{% block body %}
<div class="columns">
  <div class="column is-half">
    <h1 class="title">{{ page_title }}</h1>
    {% if form.foodbank_slug %}
      <p><a href="/admin/foodbank/{{ form.foodbank_slug }}/">&larr; Back</a></p>
    {% endif %}

    {% if error %}
      <div class="notification is-danger is-light">{{ error }}</div>
    {% endif %}

    <form method="post" action="">
      <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">

      <div class="field">
        <label class="label">Food Bank Slug</label>
        <div class="control">
          <input class="input" type="text" name="foodbank_slug" value="{{ form.foodbank_slug }}" placeholder="(none)">
        </div>
        <p class="help">Leave blank to leave this need unassigned to any food bank. A need cannot be published without one.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <label class="label">Needs</label>
        <div class="control">
          <textarea class="textarea" name="change_text" rows="6">{{ form.change_text }}</textarea>
        </div>
        <p class="help">One item per line.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <label class="label">Excess</label>
        <div class="control">
          <textarea class="textarea" name="excess_change_text" rows="6">{{ form.excess_change_text }}</textarea>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <div class="control">
          <label class="checkbox"><input type="checkbox" name="published" value="1"{% if form.published %} checked{% endif %}> Published</label>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <div class="control">
          <button type="submit" class="button is-link is-light" onclick="this.form.submit();this.disabled = true;">Save</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </form>
  </div>

  {% if show_preview %}
    <div class="column is-half">
      <iframe class="preview-frame" src="/admin/proxy/?foodbank={{ form.foodbank_slug }}&amp;field=url" style="width:100%;height:1000px;border:none;" loading="lazy"></iframe>
    </div>
  {% endif %}
</div>
{% endblock %}
